    {
      "type": "Text",
      "props": {
        "id": "Text-4df9fa1d-d0d8-4687-bf74-72583b9a040b",
        "text": "<p>Gangireddu is a harvesting festival of Andhra Pradesh. It means decorated Ox. People of the nomadic tribe- Jangam, receive old oxen from the farmers, who are unfit for farming. After decorating the Ox, they go door to door playing trumpet and the ox dancing. People consider them auspicious, thus in return they give him food, clothes and money.</p>",
        "style": "body",
        "align": "start",
        "measure": "normal",
        "layout": {
          "width": "text",
          "space": "none",
          "show": "all",
          "motion": "none"
        }
      }
    },
